{
  "_readme": [
    "Where each community sits on a map.",
    "",
    "This file is reference data, not live data: it ships with the code, is",
    "reviewed like code, and a correction is an edit and a push. That is on",
    "purpose — a pin in the wrong state is the one failure this feature cannot",
    "have, and putting it here means every change to it is visible in a diff.",
    "",
    "Coordinates are NOT derived from the community name at runtime. Of the 39",
    "names, 14 carry no city at all and 9 of those name a development rather",
    "than a town: 'The Goldton At Lake Nona' is in Orlando, 'Tribute at Melford'",
    "is in Bowie, 'The Oscar at Veramendi' is in New Braunfels. Two more are",
    "ambiguous across states — there is an Athens in Georgia, Alabama and",
    "Tennessee, and a Madison in Alabama, Mississippi and Wisconsin. Guessing",
    "would be right most of the time and confidently wrong the rest, which on a",
    "map nobody questions.",
    "",
    "'verified' is false on every entry until a person who knows the community",
    "has looked at the pin and agreed with it. Anything still false is a",
    "proposal, and the map says so.",
    "",
    "A community missing from this file is not drawn and IS counted. It never",
    "gets an approximate position 'for now'."
  ],
